    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="0587" n="575" xml:id="pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859B.20/7–2045</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Danish
                        Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kauffmann</hi>)<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d570-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-25">July 25, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to request that the areas
                    in Greenland appearing on the attached list shall be considered as defense areas
                    in accordance with the provisions of Article V of the Agreement between Denmark
                    and the United States for the defense of Greenland which was signed on April 9,
                    1941.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed.]</closer>


                <xi:include href="d570-a1.xml" xpointer="d570-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d570-f1" n="47" type="source" xml:id="d570-f1-content">
                <p>In his note dated July 31, 1945, the Danish Minister acknowledged receipt of the
                    Acting Secretary’s note and stated that he had immediately taken steps to bring
                    the contents of the note to the knowledge of the Danish Government
                    (859B.20/7–3145).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
